{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"9e4fd76649f01d32","type":"text","text":"\n# Lore Brainstorming:\n--- \nShinigami kun\n* Prefers his new life as a Shinigami. \n\t* He likes the feeling of being untouchable and having the freedom to do whatever he wants\n* Prized possession is the letter Saburou wrote to him before death. He doesn't have it anymore, but he has at least half of it memorized.\n* Can eat, but only when offered food through people who have a connection with him (can't have him be too ghost-ly now. He must still be bound by the rules of death)\n\t* Could be a good view into what dead people are like in Ite, since we have two ghosts. Nozaki-chan would prolly be able to bend the rules thanks to her lineage tho\n* Super squeamish about copepods, crabs, and the like. Almost pathetically so.\n\n\nShinigami Lore\n* Not psychopomps (?), makes the candle thing kinda obselete\n\t* Though Shinigami nowadays are understood to be grim reapers\n* Cave of candles \n\t* Tbh this part isn't particularly Japanese, since it was imported from a western story. Struggling to incorporate it into the story. I'm thinking it's something specific to the Hiue family tho (like flame rising)\n\t\t* Maybe it can be like a thing in the underworld\n\t\t* The Hiues are in charge of it, of course (hiue = rising flame)\n\t* Maybe it has something to do with the family Kami (jellyfish hero or smth idk. Managed to strike down a turtle all on her lonesome with such speed she caught on ocean fire. Jellyfish Fireball much?)\n\t\t* Pities her descendants and the awful tradition, but feels its necessary because weak jellyfish can't protect shit.\n\t\t\t* Many turn into youkai because of it, and she has the ones that *can* pass on hunt them down so they don't cause harm to future descendants or other Jellyfish (which she will not tolerate)\n\t\t\t* Maybe Shinigami kun possesses Shinki so that he can escape them? \n\t\t\t\t* He's different from other Shinigami, who kill because it's the life order. He's specifically a renegade shinigami. \n\t\t\t\t\t* Messing up with the life order would get Shinigami kun found out immediately AND in trouble with the underworld gods tho, so he advises Shinki not to break the rules of death.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* \"If they're at the foot of the bed, they're just messing with someone, and you can drive them away. Otherwise, do NOT do anything.\"\n\t\t\t\t* WAIIIIT What if he originally pretended he passed peacefully to get access to the candle, and stole Jirou's candle. \n\t\t\t\t\t* Couldn't Shinigami kun have just blew out Jirou's candle(?) (No, I want him to see my face as he dies). He's in this for spiteful revenge\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* Tbh maybe the candles can't be blown out. They'll keep burning until the candle is gone. That's the hiue way (forever rising fire ehe)\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* The only way he could do this was replace the candles with someone whose remaining lifespan was fairly short- and found Shinki by chance. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t* Her greed set the scene. He could use this to get to Jirou.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* Also lowk maybe candles are tied to the person they're for, so Shinigami kun can take it out if Shinki for the scene. \n\t\t\t\t\t* He takes Shinki into hell to escape because now the ppl in charge of hell are after the both of them for breaking the rules.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* He's mad at her for breaking the rules and for not trusting him. Shinki is like \"well, it's not like we were making an honest living doing what you were doing and I needed to move on to better opportunities.\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* Shinigami kun is like \"You're really going to be like this now? Look at this- this used to be *his* candle! When you revived him you switched your lifespans! Well? Was it worth the money you got from it?\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* Shinki panics because no- she can't die like this, and then she begs a spiteful shinigami kun for a way out. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t* Time is running out. He knows he and Shinki are going to get caught- and right now, the first and last thing he wants to do is help her.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t* Also tbh he knew he was gonna get caught when Jirou died since the Hiue line is monitored closely- but he didn't expect to care that Shinki got caught up in all of it\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t* Once a light it goes out it can't be reversed\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* He stamps out the flame in Jirou's candle. It won't make it go out forever, but he'll go into a coma and Shinki can use it to replace her light.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* \"Just so you know, I'm not doing this because I care about you. I'm only doing this because I hate my brother a lot more than I hate you right now\" (he's in denial about his feelings of betrayal)\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* \n\t\t\t\t* Chose Shinki because when he possessed her, her drive to make money won over her drive to die\n\t\t\t\t\t* So it's kinda like, mutual I guess? Shinigami kun needs her to be alive to hide, and Shinki needs to make money for her goals and also so she doesn't succumb to shinigami things\n\t\t\t\t* Chose Shinki because he could see her candle was going to go out relatively soon (but not so soon that he wouldn't have a chance to kill Jirou)\n\t\t\t\t\t* Convenience! Also she was funny.\n\t\t\t\t\t* ALSO, that would mean he really wants to save her. Though uh, why didn't he just tell her everything before she acted herself? \n\t\t\t\t\t\t* Shinki fatal flaw: Blinded by money. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t* Shinigami kun: Tells her that Jirou is his brother and that he wants to replace his candle with hers. So no matter what, do not heal him. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t* What if he just tells her to not heal Jirou no matter what, and not about the candle thing? (It's about trust baybee, that makes the betrayal hurt more ^-^)\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t* Either way is a win-win for him. Shinigami kun is a very spiteful jelly\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t* If Shinki manages to light it: He'll follow her and kill her spitefully.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t* Also either way Shinki lowk made bad blood with the Hiue family, she's gonna change her name and run away anyways(?)\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t* If Shinki blows it out: He'll just snuff Jirou's candle next\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t* Lowk ig this means Katsuo is raised by his bio mother since his dad is definitely not making out of this one alive.\n\t\t\t\t* Either that or I scrap the tsukimono kill thing and Shinigami just possesses her because she's convenient and interesting. (it's ok to do this btw, it happens in the rakugo)\n\t\t* Maybe the Hiues as Shinigami are fucking terrifying? Like king of the hill kinda terrifying (nah, continuity issues)\n\t\t\t* (But then why can't he just drive all the shinigami away?)\n\t\t\t\t* Balance thing? \n\t\t\t* What happened to the other Hiues?\n\t\t\t\t* They all passed on, I think. \n\t\t\t* Past hiues definitely can't mess with hiues that are alive. That defeats the whole purpose of the tradition\n* Maybe he died in a way that made him into a shinigami, rather than allowing him to pass on (nah, the ancestor  idea is better)\n\t* tbf i'm sure the other siblings also passed in traumatic ways. \n\t\t* Candle candle candle \n\t* ... bro i'm already back to square one lol. This was the idea before ??? \n\t\t* It just has to be way worse than how his siblings died\n\t\t* Jiro killed him but also tormented him because they had reaaally bad blood.\n\t\t\t* Destroyed his letter in a fire in front of him? \n\t\t\t\t* Incinerated? (Hiues that die this way get a special )\n\t\t\t* Electricity?\n\t\t\t* Firing squad (boring)\n\t\t\t* Lethal injection?\n\t\t\t* Pinned him to the wall with nails and shot/sliced\n\t\t\t* Boiled alive?\n\t\t* Locked/locked in a room and eaten alive by parasites (... 👀). Maybe it's one of Futao's special torture methods that he wanted to test out lowk. Reason why he finds Shinki is because he has vertical migration unlocked\n\t\t\t* Jirou went to such lengths Futao suggested it on a whim. He thinks it's fitting because Shirou fucked around a lot and he has no respect for him.\n\t\t\t* wait holy shit kuru kuru kurikaesu (Shirou learns that they both turn on him, he tries to escape but instead gets lost in the underbelly of the governmental structure)\n\t\t\t\t* The test subjects are like 3 years old atp. I could maybe foreshadow them\n\t\t\t* This is just giving a cruel game of cat and mouse. \n* ","x":280,"y":-1860,"width":1340,"height":1720},
		{"id":"725aea3cc1f67f0e","type":"text","text":"Rakugo notes\n---\n- Man dies because switching the futon switched his life with the dying man's life.\n- The shinigami going \"Hora? Hora hora horaaaaa?\" while the man's candle is going out is very funny and I think I need to put that in \n- The meta is that feet = life, head = death\n- The candles are just a part of the meta. The story doesn't really explain where all the candles come from or where the shinigami takes the protag\n\t- Making the hikurages in charge of keeping track of lifespan would be cool ig. Maybe they make candles\n- Would make sense for chironex to be in charge of that since they have the highest kill count\n- \"I hope you sold your life for a good price.\"","x":687,"y":-38,"width":593,"height":518},
		{"id":"1fc043d9080ac846","type":"text","text":"Shinki swaps her own lifespan with Jirou's?","x":1400,"y":160,"width":340,"height":80},
