		{"id":"f6ad27cd671b1c3e","type":"text","text":"# Ideas for Patients\n--- \n- First Client: \n\t- Super wealthy. Kinda an asshole. Maybe a pain in the ass in Ite lowk\n\t- \"I can't thank you enough. The gift of life you've given me is priceless\"\n\t- \"You can start by giving me money.\"\n\t- \"Ah... right, this should be enough...\" (gives her 30k)\n\t- *God, this jellyfish is definitely out of touch... I'll happily take the money though.*\n- Nozaki Family:\n\t- Maybe Yuune? Or maybe Shinigami kun just notices her in the corner and notes how something is off about her (atp she's very young).\n- Futao / Kazuo:\n\t- Fakeout cause lowk that's what did in the guy in the grimm's fairytale.\n- Hiue Family:\n\t- Jirou with the disease in his balls\n\t- Katsuo keeps floating over to him. lol.\n- Moon Jellyfish \n\t- Inverted bell\n\t- Rough shape\n\t- One of these is Sui maybe? \n- Red lantern jellyfish ?\n- Hanakari jellyfish ? (same genus, dif species as prev)\n- Urashima kurage (*urashimea globosa*)\n- Kami kurage (*Spirocodon salator*)\n- Yamaguchi (Shinigami kun has interesting dialog if you choose this one)\n\t- Teri has 2 older siblings, but he is 16 atp.\n\t- Oh lowk the light novel happens around this time. Maybe we can get some of Shima's art as an easter egg\n- Akakurage (*Chrysaora pacifica*)\n- *Mastigias papua*\n- Other *Cassiopea ornata*s\n- *Nemophilema nomurai*\n- Bizen Kurage (*Rhopilema esculentum*)\n- Ebikurage (*Netrostoma setouchiana*)\n- Murasaki Kurage (*Thysanostoma*)\n- Jellyfish from the Kyoto Suizokukan\n\t- Black Kurage\n\t- One of Achlys' godmothers(?) (ik they're *Chrysaora melanaster* but the point still stands)\n- Okikurage\n\t- One of Naito's older siblings? Maybe it gets her to start drawing because she's so sad\n- Andon kurage (*Carybdea brevipedalia*)\n- *Aequora sp* (There's many different species in Japan)\n- Hanagasa kurage\n\t- Taka Ryuu's Aunt\n\t- lowk imply that he was the one who killed her(?)\n\t- Anyways you can't heal her. \n- *Craspedacusta sowerbyi*\n\nNote: I wanna shoot for at least [x] amount of clients","x":22,"y":-3504,"width":1200,"height":1160},
		{"id":"8929f0ea1f571fbc","type":"text","text":"# Ailments\n- Parasites, physical damage\n\t- Hole/ rips in bell, tentacles, broken \n\t- Apparently bacteria can eat holes or disintegrate (moon) jellyfish within 48 hours\n- Poison\n\t- coral/anemone/bigger jellyfish poison (Shinigami kun can relate)\n\t- Heavy metal pollution\n- No explanation\n\t- Weakness (very little pulse)\n\t- Not eating\n- Eversion\n\t- Not a big issue since jellyfish are sapient, but it does render them unable to eat on their own\n- Balling (Inversion)\n\t- Caused by trauma, water chemistry, or improper water flow\n- Magnesium Chloride(?)\n\n[for more ideas on ailments](http://www.jellyfishcare.com/)\n\n[Jellyfish Care Handbook (AZA) Ch7 p39](https://assets.speakcdn.com/assets/2332/aza_jellyfish_care_manual.pdf)","x":1262,"y":-3464,"width":318,"height":840},
		{"id":"ba3c581d45a04c31","type":"text","text":"big cities tend to have dead zone issues unless they plant lots of algae and stuff","x":1512,"y":-3520,"width":250,"height":112},
		{"id":"5656eb2d68c6eecc","type":"text","text":"Jellyfish disease isn't well-studied in the present day. maybe the [[The Sakasai Family]] also does a lot of pharmaceutical stuff?\n\nShinki must feel pretty powerful healing ailments her family hasn't been able to heal.\n- (With the wave of a tentacle, I can do the work of god...)\nGranted she's just driving out shinigamis but shhh no one needs to know","x":1629,"y":-3165,"width":250,"height":481},
		{"id":"40e6c237fc0fcecb","type":"text","text":"---\n\n---\nshinigami kun and exorcism\n---\n- He gives Shinki the ability to see Shinigami\n\t- there's a death note joke in here SOMEWHERE\n- ","x":1082,"y":-2463,"width":547,"height":239},
		{"id":"816f2d5ddd911ff0","type":"text","text":"# Management Sim part\n--- \n* Rounds span a week. Each round has x turns.\n    *  General Round things:\n    \t* Beginning of Round: Advertise, Customize office, Go Shopping\n\t    \t* *(Allow player to choose prices after the first round?)*\n\t\t    \t* Or even better, allow players to choose what kind of fees to tack on (each fee lowers the chance of success)\n        \t* Certain items make the game easier, boost your chances of feet shinigami, or are just requests from Shinigami kun\n\t        \t* Money Omamori: 500 yen\n        * Middle of Round: Go to different places, heal or refuse.\n        * End of Round: Hang out with Shinigami kun (Affection meter maybe? Or satisfaction meter ig. This is required or else he will leave. Maybe). Some events require money\n        * You can only choose up to 5 clients per round. You can choose them from a pool of 10 though\n\t        * Maybe there's an item that lets you choose up to 7 per round? (or maybe that's just the advertising)\n\t        * (Might not keep this)\n    * Nozaki Family are a forced event and will come depending on your money threshold during a round, or will come when you buy a certain item\n\t    * OR, maybe they'll just show up on your list in the 4th week and you can just completely skip them if you want. But maybe they'll pay like, a lot of money or they'll offer the player something super valuable in return\n\t\t    * Or maybe Shinki will mention that they own a shrine when she pulls up the phone and Shinigami kun will be like \"Ugh, those places ick me out. Maybe you should avoid them.\"\n\t\t    * Another Idea:\n\t\t\t    * They give you a little talisman that lets you drive any Shinigami kun out temporarily, as a free gift for every route (discretely, without him knowing). \n\t\t\t    * You can use it on a failed exorcism, but you should save it for the Hiue family(?) (atp i think that's too many moving parts tho)\n    *  Have a vitality meter? \n\t    * Round ends when you run out. After each round you start with less and less of it.\n\t\t    * Make this look vaguely like a candle. But not so much that it's obvious to players. It'll be like a generic energy bar thing\n\t\t\t    * Maybe when it goes down it'll look like melting\n\t\t    * Taking jobs makes it go lower by a set amount.\n\t\t    * Hanging out with Shinigami kun also makes it lower by a set amount (albeit smaller. He *is* a shinigami, after all. Even if he isn't actively killing you)\n\t    * The more jobs you take, the less vitality you have in the next round\n\t\t    * I wonder why...\n\t* Exorcism part\n\t\t* Maybe it'll be like undertale where you just have to hit the target\n\t\t\t* The bonuses you buy can make this easier or harder, but at some point you'll just be fighting against chance \n\t\t\t\t* Wait... this is not a bad idea. Have a secret value hidden from the player. \n\t\t\t\t* Have the spell\n\t\t\t* \n\t\t* Or we can just take out skill entirely and just have the player look for the shinigami with shinigami eyes(?)\n\t\t\t* Ofc we can hear a clip of someone saying the spell and allow the player to hit a button to emulate clapping\n* Hiue Family    \n\t* Fatal disease in the balls. I'm joking that it's caused by Shinigami kun but he did really want it to happen.\n    * Shinigami kun wants to go only so he can be the one to do his brother in. \n    * Shinki goes, but then decides to work with Jirou and tricks Shinigami kun- (who gets driven away maybe).\n\t    * Time skip, after a while the amount of headside shinigami increases and Shinki can't make money anymore, she's desperate. \n\t\t    * Takes the Hiue job. Shinigami kun just wants to do him in.\n\t\t\t    * He knows he'll be caught here, but he just wants revenge. Jirou was fated to die early, anyways. \n\t\t    * Jirou's second wife is on the bedside. Shinki gets promised funding for a business deal if she can at least save his life for a little longer.. She can't refuse. \n\t\t    * She remembers the spell the Nozakis taught her to rid herself of Shinigami kun. She does that, and Shinigami kun is driven out\n\t\t\t    * Or actually it's just the same spell and Shinki gets a relic that makes it work on Shinigami kun.\n\t\t    * Shinigami kun is... driven out. (side)\n\t\t    * She gets the deal, leaves, and finds Shinigami kun waiting out front. \"You think that cheap piece of fabric could do me in for good? God, you're so stupid\"\n\t\t    * Grabs her by the wrist, and brings her down to his secret little cave, with a single candle. \n\t\t\t    * Grabs Shinki's candle from her heart.\n\t    * Idk, maybe if you go bankrupt before the 5th month, you're forced to take the Hiue family job and that leads to the worst ending(?)\n\t\t    * If you're forced to take the Hiue job, then the ending changes depending on when you go bankrupt\n\t\t\t    * 1st week: Worst ending. Shinigami kun blows out the candle for you. Shinigami kun also won't say much about Jirou other than that he hates him.\n\t\t\t    * 2nd week: \n\t\t* \n    * She gets thanked, etc etc, and then when she leaves the building she sees Shinigami kun waiting outside\n    * Gets dragged out to the underworld and sees the candles. See [[The Shinigami that is also a Jellyfish#Endings (most result in you becoming a shinigami)|Endings]]\n- List of rounds: \n\t- Round 1: \n\t\t- Right after Shinki finishes the tutorial. She doesn't have enough money for an apartment so she lives in a net cafe for the time being  \n\t\t- Lowk this is a good time for a general game tutorial since there isn't much to do other than make money (general idea of how the menus work) \n- Numbers by round\n\n| Round |     | Payment* | Available Events                                                                  | Special Items to Buy                                                                                                                                      |\n| ----- | --- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 1     |     | 5-10k    | <br>- Read Manga<br>- Conbini run<br>- Surf the web<br>- Play in the park<br>     | - New clothes (for Shinigami san): 4.5k<br>   - They make him happier ig<br>- New clothes (for Shinki): 3.5k<br>   - (they give you a 1k boost in profit) |\n| 2     |     | 10-15k   |                                                                                   | - Apartment                                                                                                                                               |\n| 3     |     | 10-17k   | - \"Please give me your customer service smile\"<br>   - Player can choose yes / no |                                                                                                                                                           |\n| 4     |     | 15-20k   |                                                                                   |                                                                                                                                                           |\n| 5     |     | 15-30k   |                                                                                   |                                                                                                                                                           |\n*\\*Anything above the cap will be a guaranteed fail*","x":-2350,"y":-1187,"width":1540,"height":2160},
		{"id":"de8c2f68e873d101","type":"text","text":"### Beginning:\n--- \n* Game starts in a Rakugo Hall. Shinigami kun is telling the story, as a jellyfish. Disclaimer that everyone is a jellyfish before he becomes his Gijinka form.\n\t* Do a Rakugo bit before bowing and moving onto the next scene\n\t\n* (March 31st) Meet Shinki, a jellyfish girl recently kicked out of her house for being framed for embezzlement. She's at her lowest point, but the closer she's pushed to death the more determined she is to make money\n* Meet Shinigami kun, who wants to torment her but is fascinated by her business proposal, and agrees. Possesses Shinki.\n\n* Start quack doctor scheme (Shinki: \"If it works, is it really a scam?\")\n\t* Tutorial for quack doctor scheme. Will be used in the management sim aspect\n\t* You go into the house, see the patient in their futon. \n\t* Shinigami kun will be at the foot of the bed (ik it might not be accurate to the story but for game reasons I really want it to work like this.)\n\n\n","x":-2060,"y":-1927,"width":960,"height":620},
		{"id":"04488f0427eeb946","type":"text","text":"# Game Beats brainstorming\n---","x":-1776,"y":-2287,"width":393,"height":124,"color":"#ffa3f3"},
		{"id":"7d6014e974691bea","type":"text","text":"### Endings (most result in you dying):\n--- \n* **Love ending**: Maybe kinda yandere? Not sure. \n\t* If you do a certain amount of events. Shinki becomes his raison d'ete, but after the betrayal he decides that he'll just keep her here. Forever.\n* **Candle endings**: Have the candle scene. Hold the candle with the mouse and wait until its lit fully. \n\t* If the player moves the candle before it's //fully// lit, she will die. Shinigami kun will talk while this happens so if the player moves mouse to move along with his dialogue, they die (\"Haha. You think you could light anything with those shakey hands?\", \"It's going oooout, see seee seeeeeeee?\"). You just have to hold still and let him talk. (God. This is peak role embodiment tho, You have to ignore him)\n\t\t* Note: Maybe have the candle shake a little by itself and you have to fangangle against it? I like that better lowk\n\t\t* The shinigami will still talk but if you don't fanangle against Shinki's hands while you read then you die\n    * If player lights the candle\n    \t* 1% chance she sneezes and blows it out (get fucked lol) (rolls each time the scene is loaded for the completionists)\n        * Otherwise, Shinigami kun just claps and disappears- ending the interaction and friendship coldly.\n        * Then Shinki goes home as if nothing ever happend...\n        \t* Actually, when Shinki goes to sleep, she sees him by the head of her futon. \"Shit\"\n            * If you didn't buy ofuda (very hard, you need to make a lot of money and fight Shinki on the menuing), the game ends there. Otherwise, you slap the ofuda on him and uh, it gives you enough time to escape. \n            * The win is empty though, and you're back to square one. Now with a shinigami on your heels. Escape the country and change your name. ","x":-3710,"y":-1067,"width":1120,"height":700},
		{"id":"caeea306e19ce058","type":"text","text":"lowk tho it would make sense for the game to take a set amount of time (maybe like 3-4 months?). Don't let the game end too early.","x":-855,"y":-563,"width":250,"height":140,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"6da91c4a119417e3","type":"text","text":"# Payment\nShould be paid on avg like 25k per successful thing by the end of it.\n\nhttps://myoryuji.com/archives/29960 \n- (In Japanese) general guideline for how much harae cost. You can expect them to be 5-30k for something like healing)\n\t- Shinki isn't technically an exorcist but she'd definitely act like one\n\nhttps://alea.care/resources/cost-health-Japan: \n- cost of healthcare (i forgot why i needed this)","x":-810,"y":-1025,"width":410,"height":402},
		{"id":"df8729d65a2d2aac","type":"text","text":"Achievements\n---\n- Cheapskate: Go through the whole game without buying new clothes\n- Net Cafe Enthusiast: Never move out of the net cafe\n\t- Get a net cafe ID card in the gallery\n- Classic Ending: Blow out the candle yourself\n- Shakey Hands: Snuff out the candle right after lighting it on fire\n- Poor Ending: Have Shinigami-kun blow out the candle himself\n- Winner of Capitalism: Have more than [x] yen in the bank\n- Forbidden Love: Make the Shinigami fall in love with you","x":-700,"y":-163,"width":600,"height":446,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"1ddbab5d42cafb81","type":"text","text":"Money\n--- \n### Net Cafe\nLowk the only realworld net cafe in Kyoto that offered a 1 week plan was CocoNe net cafe. 23,990 for the mat-type room \n![[Pasted image 20260221005250.png]]\nHer first client probably gave her like 25k lowk (truly a miracle cure)\n### Apartment\n18 sq meters and 18k per month\n\nhttps://rentola.com/listings/p50f00d\n\nI think we can haggle with the price though, and it doesn't have to be 100% accurate to real japan.\n\nThough tbh 18k per month is doable considering the nature of the pay. The downpayment is just the issue (maybe Shinki haggles it down to 45k because she's just that business oriented)","x":-400,"y":-903,"width":490,"height":560},
		{"id":"f76697419cd567c3","type":"text","text":"lowk tho it would make sense for the game to take a set amount of time (maybe like 3-4 months?). Don't let the game end too early.","x":-855,"y":-343,"width":250,"height":140,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"9b96081e5814c53d","type":"text","text":"General beats of what i want to happen\n- Shinigami kun possesses Shinki\n- Shinki begins her scam business (she calls herself a doctor using \"natural\" methods)\n- Shinki gradually begins to run out of patients, and she gets desperate\n- She goes to the Hiues, and Jirou's other wife offers her shareholder support to heal him.\n\t- She can't let Katsuo be the only child in the family.\n- She heals Jirou, Shinigami kun gets mad\n- Candles happen. Shinki either dies or escapes and has to change her name or smth","x":1860,"y":-2140,"width":726,"height":329},
		{"id":"411a9bcff9df7ffc","type":"text","text":"<iframe width=\"300\" height=\"200\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/P4PCds4tlT4?si=WREJyKmAVBDLl1ZO&amp;start=174\" title=\"YouTube video player\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe>","x":1120,"y":320,"width":320,"height":231},
		{"id":"7e9d5dd763fd82e1","x":1914,"y":-679,"width":1206,"height":1039,"type":"text","text":"## Sparknotes of the shinigami lore part\nShinigami kun pretends to pass peacefully, working under the grand Hiue. However, still bitter and wanting revenge, he steals Jirou's candle and sets off to find a living mortal to replace it with. Since candles with sufficient amount of wax cannot be tampered with easily, Shinigami kun sets off to find a candle that he can swap it with.\n- Then he finds Shinki by chance, and decides she's his best chance of getting close to Jirou without getting caught (hiding behind possession)\n\t- At that point, her candle was small, but large enough to buy him time to get to Jirou\n- She wants money, and he has an idea. Give her shinigami eyes (omg like box jellyfish), and let her become a fake doctor. She'll go around, and eventually they'll find Jirou.\n\t- When a shinigami is next to a jellyfish's bell, give up.\n\t- When a shinigami is at the end of their tentacles, death isn't in their fate and I'll scare away the shinigami\n\t\t- The spell was something made up by Shinki to make it look more convincing. The quicktime event is there to give the player extra bonuses for making it look convincing to the client\n- They do their thing. Either: \n\t- A: Shinki oversleeps for one point but takes it as a sign that she's not working enough (slept a bit longer because Shinigami kun swapped candles)\n\t- B: Shinki gets deathly sick (her lifespan is approaching), and Shinigami kun swaps it before it's too late. Just before the Jirou thing happens.\n- When they're the most desperate for money- they suddenly get an offer from Jirou. Bingo. \n\t- Shinigami kun warns her not to heal him, no matter what. Shinki only gives him an empty promise. She needs money\n\t- They get there. Jirou balls don't work. Jirou's second wife promises Shinki a life-changing amount of money even just to heal him temporarily.\n\t- Shinki looks. Sees Shinigami kun at his head. \n\t- He's not here to help her now. But she\n\n* Couldn't Shinigami kun have just blew out Jirou's candle(?) (No, I want him to see my face as he dies). He's in this for spiteful revenge\n\t* Tbh maybe the candles can't be blown out. They'll keep burning until the candle is gone. That's the hiue way (forever rising fire ehe)\n\t* The only way he could do this was replace the candles with someone whose remaining lifespan was fairly short- and found Shinki by chance. \n\t\t* Her greed set the scene. He could use this to get to Jirou.\n\t* Also lowk maybe candles are tied to the person they're for, so Shinigami kun can take it out if Shinki for the scene. \n* He takes Shinki into hell to escape because now the ppl in charge of hell are after the both of them for breaking the rules.\n\t* He's mad at her for breaking the rules and for not trusting him. Shinki is like \"well, it's not like we were making an honest living doing what you were doing and I needed to move on to better opportunities.\"\n\t* Shinigami kun is like \"You're really going to be like this now? Look at this- this used to be *his* candle! When you revived him you switched your lifespans! Well? Was it worth the money you got from it?\"\n\t* Shinki panics because no- she can't die like this, and then she begs a spiteful shinigami kun for a way out. \n\t* Time is running out. He knows he and Shinki are going to get caught- and right now, the first and last thing he wants to do is help her.\n\t\t* Also tbh he knew he was gonna get caught when Jirou died since the Hiue line is monitored closely- but he didn't expect to care that Shinki got caught up in all of it\n\t\t* Once a light it goes out it can't be reversed\n\t* He stamps out the flame in Jirou's candle. It won't make it go out forever, but he'll go into a coma and Shinki can use it to replace her light.\n\t* \"Just so you know, I'm not doing this because I care about you. I'm only doing this because I hate my brother a lot more than I hate you right now\" (he's in denial about his feelings of betrayal)\n\t* "},
		{"id":"d81597a19ecf0110","type":"text","text":"Maybe he switches their candles when Shinki gets deathly ill at some point- caused by being near Shinigami kun. Feels bad about this, but he's like \"I'll heal you\", goes into another room, and she gets miraculously better.\n\"What did you do?\"\n\"Shinigami stuff. Don't worry about it.\"\n(She'd ask too many questions, and he didn't want to admit he was just using her.)\n- Does he believe they share a bond that's more than just \"boss\" and \"employee\"?","x":1720,"y":-1180,"width":720,"height":220}
	],
